{
  "id": "Compound::DB01326 - Gene::9356",
  "verbalization": "Cefamandole is implicated in the transport of organic anions across cellular membranes through its interaction with Slc22a6, as evidenced by its binding to Slc22a8 and Slc22a11, which are both involved in sodium-independent organic anion transport. This suggests that Cefamandole may influence the activity of Slc22a6, potentially by modulating the transport of anions across cell membranes. The shared involvement of Slc22a6 in the transport of anions, as seen in multiple pathways, indicates a possible functional link between Cefamandole and Slc22a6, possibly through the regulation of anion transport. The evidence from the three paths collectively supports the notion that Cefamandole may act as a modulator of Slc22a6, influencing its role in anion transport, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
